<title>USA: U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - ISSUES TO WATCH - AUG 11.</title>
<headline>U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - ISSUES TO WATCH - AUG 11.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>-- Digital Equipment Corp is seeking to sell its computer-network equipment business, the Wall Street Journal reported, citing people familiar with the situation. The unit hasestimated annual revenues of about $600 million and could fetch as much as $750 million, industry officials said. DEC stock closed at 43-15/16 Friday.</p>
<p>-- Metrocall Inc and ProNet Inc said they had signed a definitive agreement under which ProNet will merge into Metrocall, creating the second largest U.S. paging company. Metrocall will swap 0.9 share for each ProNet share. Metrocall and ProNet both closed at six.</p>
<p>-- Fairfield Communities Inc said it signed a definitive agreement to acquire Vacation Break U.S.A. Inc in a stock swap valued at about $190.2 million. Fairfield closed at 32-5/8 while Vacation Break closed at 14.</p>
<p>((--Wall Street Desk 212-859-1730))</p>
